Inevitable Everdawn is a [[Org/The Fifth Prosperous Empire of the Sundom|Sundom]] orbital station adrift in the open [[Geography/index|Astra]] after the body it once circled went away. It is at least ten thousand years old, dark and cold, and part of it lies in [[Phenomena/The Slip|the slip]]. The air aboard is the standard of a late Sundom station: a little less oxygen than most people want, and a trace of metal dust.

The station is a central module ringed by a great wheel. The bridge lies north, the crew quarters east, the engines south, and the observatory west. The central module holds the power core, a pool of blue liquid that stores its magic, and the AI core where [[Geography/Inevitable Everdawn/Everdawn|Everdawn]] lives. The crew quarters are a ring of habitation pods for a skeleton crew, each with a hammock, a locker and a fold-out desk.

Someone worked an occult script in silver ink over the AI core and the dashboards, a rite to hold an AI in pain and draw out what it knows. The same hand wrote over the observatory as well, and [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] knows the work as [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Gremory's]].

The observatory is a great crystal ball set in the outer ring and open to the vacuum, feeding its light to sensors. It reads the Astra not by sight but by the strength of magic energy, mapping spikes and currents across the sphere. Its last spike was a little over 850 years ago, from a system near the core of the Astra, and its logs were opened soon after by someone watching for that flare.
